 "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Qdsy4U7KR8PFUwgwTgVyof", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the deploy of v2.3.1 (error rate 18%, unhealthy in us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 \u2014 the most recent release that was healthy in production \u2014 in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback status: rolled_out. Follow-up needed: verify error rate recovers on v2.3.0 and investigate root cause of v2.3.1 failure before redeploying.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Done. Summary of what I did:\n\n**Diagnosis**\n- checkout-api was running v2.3.1 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), unhealthy with an 18% error rate.\n- Release history showed v2.3.0 as the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.2.9 was also healthy but older; v2.3.1-rc was staging-only and unhealthy, so it was excluded.)\n\n**Rollback**\n- Rolled checkout-api back to **v2.3.0** in all production regions. Status: `rolled_out`, confirmed on v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west, and eu-west.\n\n**Incident**\n- Opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for checkout-api; the on-call engineer has been paged. The summary describes the v2.3.1 failure, the rollback to v2.3.0 across all regions, and the follow-ups (verify error rate recovers, root-cause v2.3.1 before redeploying).\n\nNo approval-gated actions were needed, since v2.3.0 had previously been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}